# GET /ui — the page: the node's browser, in yours.
#
# Served from a gated op, not a static FILES/index.html. Static files bypass
# the rules, and so the gate in 090/095: a static page would be world-readable,
# and would load without the browser ever asking for the password (a fetch or a
# WebSocket that gets 401 does not prompt; only a top-level 401 does). Served
# here, an unauthenticated GET /ui gets 401, the browser prompts, and the
# credentials then flow to the /screen WebSocket and the fetch() calls.
#
# The page is ui.html, beside this op.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path == "/ui"
  EMIT @web.res.status = 200,
       @web.res.headers.content-type.0 = "text/html; charset=utf-8",
       @web.res.headers.cache-control.0 = "no-store",
       @web.res.body = &b64encode(&include("ui.html")),
       @halt = true
